+# Deployment Guide for Windows (PowerShell)
+
+## Step 1: Deploy to Railway
+
+```powershell
+# Push code from Windows to GitHub
+git push origin main
+```
+
+This triggers Railway's webhook to auto-deploy (should complete in 1-2 minutes).
+
+---
+
+## Step 2: Set Environment Variable on Railway
+
+1. Go to **Railway Dashboard**: https://railway.app
+2. Select your **dublin-events-app** project
+3. Click **Variables** tab
+4. Add new variable:
+   - **Key**: `SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY`
+   - **Value**: `your-secure-random-string-here` (e.g., `dublin-scraper-abc123xyz789`)
+5. Click **Deploy** to apply changes
+
+*Alternative: Use Railway CLI*
+
+```powershell
+# Login to Railway (if not already logged in)
+railway login
+
+# Navigate to project directory
+cd "C:\Users\Mo Harvey\CLAUDE PROJECTS\dublin-events-app-complete"
+
+# Set environment variable
+railway variables set SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY="your-secure-random-string"
+
+# Redeploy to apply changes
+railway up
+```
+
+---
+
+## Step 3: Test Scraper (Manual Trigger)
+
+### Option A: Using Invoke-WebRequest (PowerShell)
+
+```powershell
+# Test local scraper (if running locally)
+$response = Invoke-WebRequest `
+  -Uri "http://localhost:3000/api/scrape/midnight?key=dev-scraper-key" `
+  -Method Post `
+  -ContentType "application/json"
+
+$response.Content | ConvertFrom-Json | ConvertTo-Json
+
+# Response should show: 6 venues, event counts, success status
+```
+
+### Option B: Using Curl (if installed)
+
+```powershell
+# Test live scraper on Railway
+curl -X POST "https://yourapp.railway.app/api/scrape/midnight?key=your-secret-key"
+
+# Response example:
+# {
+#   "success": true,
+#   "message": "✅ All 6 venues scraped successfully! Found 47 events.",
+#   "timestamp": "2026-10-01T00:15:30.000Z",
+#   "summary": {
+#     "totalVenues": 6,
+#     "successfulVenues": 6,
+#     "failedVenues": 0,
+#     "totalEventsScraped": 47,
+#     "durationMs": 8250
+#   }
+# }
+```
+
+### Option C: Using Invoke-RestMethod (PowerShell - Recommended)
+
+```powershell
+# Replace YOUR_SECRET_KEY with actual value
+$secretKey = "your-secret-key"
+$appUrl = "https://yourapp.railway.app"
+
+# Build URL
+$scraperUrl = "$appUrl/api/scrape/midnight?key=$secretKey"
+
+# Make request
+try {
+    $response = Invoke-RestMethod `
+        -Uri $scraperUrl `
+        -Method Post `
+        -ContentType "application/json" `
+        -TimeoutSec 60
+
+    # Display results
+    Write-Host "✅ Scraper Response:" -ForegroundColor Green
+    $response | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5 | Write-Host
+
+    # Extract summary
+    Write-Host "`n📊 Summary:" -ForegroundColor Cyan
+    Write-Host "Total Venues: $($response.summary.totalVenues)"
+    Write-Host "Successful: $($response.summary.successfulVenues)"
+    Write-Host "Failed: $($response.summary.failedVenues)"
+    Write-Host "Events Found: $($response.summary.totalEventsScraped)"
+    Write-Host "Duration: $($response.summary.durationMs)ms"
+
+} catch {
+    Write-Host "❌ Error: $($_.Exception.Message)" -ForegroundColor Red
+    Write-Host "Response: $($_.ErrorDetails.Message)" -ForegroundColor Red
+}
+```
+
