+## Step 4: Set Up Automated Midnight Runs
+
+### Option A: EasyCron (Easiest - Recommended)
+
+1. Visit: https://www.easycron.com/
+2. Sign up (free account)
+3. Click **Add Cron Job**
+4. Fill in details:
+   ```
+   Cron Expression: 0 0 * * *
+   Timezone:       UTC (or choose Dublin if available)
+   HTTP Method:    GET or POST
+   URL:            https://yourapp.railway.app/api/scrape/midnight?key=YOUR_SECRET_KEY
+   ```
+5. Click **Save**
+
+EasyCron will now call your scraper endpoint every night at midnight.
+
+**To verify:**
+- EasyCron shows "Execution History" with timestamps
+- Check Railway logs for scraper execution
+- Check database for new events appearing each morning
+
+### Option B: GitHub Actions (Secure - Recommended for teams)
+
+1. Create file: `.github/workflows/midnight-scrape.yml`
+
+```yaml
+name: Midnight Dublin Events Scraper
+
+on:
+  schedule:
+    # Runs at midnight UTC every day
+    - cron: '0 0 * * *'
+  
+  # Allow manual trigger from GitHub Actions tab
+  workflow_dispatch:
+
+jobs:
+  scrape:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    
+    steps:
+      - name: Trigger Dublin Events Scraper
+        run: |
+          curl -X POST "https://yourapp.railway.app/api/scrape/midnight?key=${{ secrets.SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY }}"
+        env:
+          SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY: ${{ secrets.SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY }}
+```
+
+2. Add GitHub Actions secret:
+   - Go to **Repository Settings** → **Secrets and variables** → **Actions**
+   - Click **New repository secret**
+   - Name: `SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY`
+   - Value: Your actual secret key
+
+3. Commit and push:
+```powershell
+git add .github/workflows/midnight-scrape.yml
+git commit -m "Add automated midnight scraper workflow"
+git push origin main
+```
+
+4. Verify in GitHub:
+   - Go to **Actions** tab
+   - Should see "Midnight Dublin Events Scraper" workflow
+   - It will run automatically at midnight UTC daily
+
+### Option C: Railway Scheduled Jobs (if available)
+
+Contact Railway support to see if your plan includes scheduled jobs. If so:
+1. Provide them your scraper endpoint URL
+2. They configure it to run at midnight
+3. No additional setup needed
+
