+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Scraper returns 401 Unauthorized
+**Problem:** Wrong SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY  
+**Solution:** Double-check the key matches in Railway variables
+
+### Scraper returns 0 events
+**Problem:** Venue website selectors may have changed  
+**Solution:** See SCRAPER_SETUP.md → Troubleshooting → "Scraper Returns 0 Events"
+
+### Images not displaying
+**Problem:** Image URLs not venue-domain hosted  
+**Solution:** Verify URLs in database: `SELECT image_url FROM "Event" LIMIT 5;`
+
+### Cron job not running at midnight
+**Problem:** Timezone mismatch or scheduler not set up  
+**Solution:** Check EasyCron execution history or GitHub Actions logs
+
+---
+
+## Windows-Specific Tips
+
+### Install curl (if not already installed)
+```powershell
+# Windows 10/11 usually has curl built-in
+curl --version
+
+# If not, install via Chocolatey:
+choco install curl
+```
+
+### Install Railway CLI
+```powershell
+# Via npm (requires Node.js)
+npm install -g @railway/cli
+
+# Verify installation
+railway --version
+
+# Login
+railway login
+```
+
+### Scheduled Task (Alternative to EasyCron)
+
+Instead of EasyCron, you can use Windows Task Scheduler:
+
+1. Open **Task Scheduler**
+2. Create Basic Task:
+   - Name: "Dublin Events Scraper"
+   - Trigger: Daily at 12:00 AM (midnight)
+   - Action: Start a program
+     - Program: `powershell.exe`
+     - Arguments: `-Command "Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'https://yourapp.railway.app/api/scrape/midnight?key=YOUR_SECRET_KEY' -Method Post"`
+
